.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
a network endpoint that can initiate a connection 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNetClient\fP is part of the PDG Engine's custom protocol for games\&. It handles protocol negotiation and optional connections\&. It establishes both a TCP connection (reliable transport with guaranteed delivery) and UDP communications (small and unreliable but fast) with the server\&.

.PP
On iOS JavaScriptCore, \fBNetClient\fP connects to existing PDG TCP/UDP servers using host and port\&. hasNetwork and hasNetworkClient are true; hasNetworkServer is false and \fBNetServer\fP is unavailable\&. UDP uses the TCP local endpoint; sendDgram() uses TCP until UDP negotiation succeeds, when UDP becomes unavailable, or for serialized messages larger than 1492 bytes\&. Pass {noDatagram: true} to the constructor to disable UDP\&.

.PP
Callbacks run on the engine's JavaScript thread\&. Entering the background closes connections and reports ERR_NETWORK_BACKGROUND through \fBonError()\fP; onClose() runs when the engine resumes\&. Reconnect explicitly when the application becomes active\&. No automatic reconnect occurs\&. Native TCP/UDP is unencrypted; \fBNetConnection\&.secure\fP is false for native transport\&. iOS also supports WebSocket: pass webSocketUrl or transportPolicy: "websocket-only" to connect to a PDG WebSocket listener\&. WSS uses the iOS certificate trust store and reports secure as true; ws:// requires secure: false\&. Custom tls options are unsupported on iOS\&. WebSocket sendDgram() uses reliable delivery and hasDgram remains false\&. The server must allow clients without a browser Origin header\&.

.PP
Desktop, Node and iOS also support WebTransport\&. Supply webTransportUrl and transportPolicy:"webtransport-required" to require its TLS reliable stream and optional datagrams\&. Browser auto mode attempts WebTransport before WebSocket\&. See \fBwebsocket_client_options\fP for deadlines, fallback and certificate hashes\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Apps connecting to a server on the local network must supply an NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription in their Info\&.plist\&. The OS controls permission\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNetClient\fP doesn't actually handle network communication, it only establishes the connection\&. Once established, it creates \fBNetConnection\fP objects you can use to send and receive data\&.

.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
\fBNetClient\fP, \fBNetServer\fP, and \fBNetConnection\fP all work together over a custom protocol\&. Do not attempt to use \fBNetClient\fP to connect to other kinds of servers, such as HTTP or raw TCP sockets\&. There are perfectly fine \fRNet\fP and \fRHTTP\fP modules built-in to Node\&.js (and thus to PDG) for that\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBNetConnection\fP 

.PP
\fBNetServer\fP 

.PP
\fRNode\&.js Net module\fP 

.PP
\fRNode\&.js HTTP module\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
