.SS "NetClient (\fBNetClientOptions\fP opt = \fRnull\fP)"

.PP
constructor for \fBNetClient\fP, sets client options Construct a new \fBNetClient\fP with particular options or using default values if no options are specified\&.

.PP
Available options are:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
noDatagram - flag to indicate that we should not try to establish UDP communication with the server (defaults to false, allowing UDP)
.PP

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIopt\fP A \fBNetClientOptions\fP record, or null to use the defaults\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
var myClient = new pdg\&.NetClient( {noDatagram: true} );
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
Referenced by \fBconnect()\fP, and \fBonError()\fP\&.
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBNetClient\fP connect (\fBNetServerAddress\fP serverInfo, function callback, string clientKey = \fR''\fP)"

.PP
connect to a server for your game Connect to a PDG server and complete its authentication and version handshake\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fRcallback:\fP \fBNetConnectCallback\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
The callback receives one \fBNetConnection\fP after the handshake completes\&. Errors go to \fBonError()\fP\&. WebSocket and WebTransport connections carry the same serialized messages as native TCP\&. sendDgram() uses reliable delivery on WebSocket\&. Authentication failures close the attempt; they never start another connection automatically\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIserverInfo\fP Connection settings in \fBwebsocket_client_options\fP\&. 
.br
\fIcallback\fP Function receiving the established \fBNetConnection\fP\&. 
.br
\fIclientKey\fP Optional reservation key sent before protocol negotiation\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBNetClient\fP for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
 
.PP
\fBClient connection options\fP
.RS 4

.RE
.PP
Field  Default  Meaning  host, port  Required for native TCP  Native server hostname and port\&. For WebSocket, host may be used to derive the URL\&.  transportPolicy  "auto"  Desktop, Node and iOS preserve TCP unless a web URL is supplied\&. Browsers try WebTransport, then WebSocket\&. An explicit webTransportUrl selects WebTransport in native auto mode\&. "webtransport-required" forbids fallback; "websocket-only" selects WebSocket; "native-only" rejects browser use\&.  webSocketUrl  Derived  Explicit wss:// URL\&. Native auto mode selects WebSocket when only this web URL is supplied\&. Browser auto mode derives its initial HTTPS WebTransport URL from this URL when webTransportUrl is omitted\&.  webTransportUrl  Derived  HTTPS WebTransport URL\&. Derived from host, webPort and webPath, or the browser webSocketUrl\&. Requires an HTTP/3 WebTransport listener\&.  serverCertificateHashes  Omitted  Optional array of {algorithm:"sha-256", value:Uint8Array or ArrayBuffer} entries, each containing a 32-byte SHA-256 DER certificate digest from a trusted bootstrap\&. Requires a currently valid EC certificate with validity no longer than 14 days\&. These hashes authenticate the server certificate; the PDG client key still authenticates the client\&.  webTransportTimeout  1500  Milliseconds allocated to the initial WebTransport attempt in auto mode, within the overall timeout\&.  capabilityCacheTimeout  30000  Milliseconds to cache an unsupported or timed-out WebTransport endpoint\&. 0 disables caching\&. The cache is bounded and keyed by endpoint and trust configuration\&.  webPort, webPath  5443, "/pdg"  Derived endpoint is wss://host:webPort/webPath\&.  secure  true  false permits an explicit ws:// development endpoint\&. HTTPS pages always require wss://\&.  timeout  5000 for web transports and iOS  Overall connection and PDG handshake deadline in milliseconds for web transports\&. On desktop/Node TCP, applies only when supplied\&.  handshakeTimeout  timeout or 5000  PDG handshake deadline in milliseconds; web transports also respect the remaining overall timeout\&.  maxFrameSize  1048576  Maximum reliable payload size in bytes\&.  maxPendingBytes  4194304  Maximum retained input and pending transport output bytes\&. WebSocket output overflow reports ERR_BACKPRESSURE; WebTransport overflow reports ERR_BACKPRESSURE; iOS TCP/WebSocket overflow reports ERR_NETWORK_BACKPRESSURE\&. iOS accepts 1024 to 67108864 bytes and also bounds queued events and writes to 256 each\&.  tls  Platform defaults  Native WebSocket client TLS settings, such as ca for a private certificate authority\&. WebTransport uses the platform trust store on Apple/Windows and the system CA bundle on Linux, or native tls\&.caFile for a private CA\&. Browser TLS uses platform trust\&. iOS WebSocket rejects custom tls options\&.  

.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The server must permit the page's origin and offer the pdg-net-v1 WebSocket subprotocol\&. Production endpoints need a trusted certificate and a proxy that forwards WebSocket upgrades\&. WebTransport requires UDP access to the HTTPS endpoint port\&. WebSocket uses TCP\&. Native WebTransport clients have no browser Origin; permit the empty string in the listener allowedOrigins\&.
.RE
.PP
Auto mode falls back only for unavailable WebTransport, an explicitly unsupported endpoint, or establishment timeout, before the PDG handshake begins\&. Certificate, pin, authentication, and protocol failures are terminal\&. Browsers often report opaque failures; these are terminal rather than treated as unsupported\&. No fallback occurs after a transport has been selected or a session has connected\&.

.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const client = new pdg\&.NetClient();
client\&.onError(error => console\&.error(error\&.code, error\&.message));
client\&.connect({webSocketUrl: "wss://game\&.example\&.com/pdg"}, connection => {
    connection\&.onMessage((message, connection, delivery) => {
        console\&.log(message, delivery, connection\&.transport);
    });
    connection\&.send({join: "lobby"});
}, "reservation\-key");

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBNetConnection\fP, \fBonError()\fP, \fBNetServer::expectClient()\fP 
.RE
.PP

