.SH "Member Data Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "object connection"

.PP
reference to the \fBNetConnection\fP, or boolean false if not yet connected 
.PP
\fBJavaScript value\fP
.RS 4
\fR\fBNetConnection\fP\fP or \fRfalse\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
The property starts as the literal \fRfalse\fP\&. After the underlying socket connects, it holds a \fBNetConnection\fP\&. It is not a general boolean flag, and assigning a connection does not by itself mean the PDG protocol handshake has completed\&. Use the connect callback to know when the connection is ready for application messages\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
A retained connection object is not proof that its socket is still open\&. Use the connection callbacks to track disconnection and errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBNetClient::connect()\fP, \fBNetConnection\fP 
.RE
.PP


